#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082985 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81e85da-c4ce-5353-9a7b-d18daa4caf7d" :knowledge-point/title "Converting Between Exponential and Logarithmic Form With Common Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "057534f6-5144-57c1-ade0-1693dffa44e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4058" :question/problem "Express the equation $10^3 = 1\\,000$ using logarithmic notation." :question/worked-solution "The common logarithm of $a$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a = 10^x$ is equivalent to $\\log{a} = x$\n\nIf we compare $10^3 = 1\\,000$ with $10^x = a,$ we get that $a = 1\\,000$ and $x = 3.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as $\\log{1\\,000} = 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082986 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083173 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afb7f5bb-1a71-5bf5-a4a0-1354256be22b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Common Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "e9e02baa-a9bc-5f3f-af29-2bbac1dc2634" :question/math-academy-id "e-4059" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\log\\left( 10^{7}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "The common logarithm of a power of $10$ is the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log\\left(10^x\\right) = x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x =7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log\\left( 10^{7}\\right) = 7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082987 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67d294d0-542a-5332-b837-256792817dde" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Common Logarithms of Fractions and Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "34a604f1-d3e2-5746-818a-17c572ff2243" :question/math-academy-id "e-4060" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\log\\left( 0.1 \\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $0.1$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n0.1 = 10^{-1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\log\\left( 0.1 \\right) = \\log\\left(10^{-1}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm of a power of $10$ is the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log\\left(10^x\\right) = x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x = -1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log\\left( 10^{-1} \\right)= -1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082988 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60270e0c-a60c-5a5f-8993-3d8362081c8f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions Containing Common Logarithms Using a Calculator"}] :question/id #uuid "b4b8a7af-fe7c-5d8a-80f4-c997c404a889" :question/math-academy-id "e-4061" :question/problem "Rounded to $2$ decimal places, what is the value of $2\\log(7) + 5\\log(5)?$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the required expression to $2$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate steps to $5$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)+5\\operatorname{log}⁡(5) & ≈2(0.845\\,10)+5(0.698\\,97) \\\\  & =1.690\\,20+3.494\\,85 \\\\  & =5.185\\,05 \\\\  & ≈5.19.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083173 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afb7f5bb-1a71-5bf5-a4a0-1354256be22b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Common Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35a1c537-1707-54d3-98ae-af863b9980c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520070} {:answer/id #uuid "36c63ad2-e5ab-5c30-950c-3e5928c6abe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520072} {:answer/id #uuid "97afabea-2893-5176-8db1-49f34160a9b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520205} {:answer/id #uuid "abb0d127-729c-52ec-899c-f4b419e34c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520226} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e80a2a-2a90-5e03-8332-b82cf6f8f572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb0d127-729c-52ec-899c-f4b419e34c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520226} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a053ca-7dc5-596c-888f-925fbf0bae39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5c7ea95-c351-53b5-8952-0f4a790122f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-108087" :question/problem "Find the value of $2\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t)$ at $t=10.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $t=10$ into the function. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t) & =2\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡(10\\cdot 10) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=3$ and $x=2.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})=2\\cdot 3-2=4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67d294d0-542a-5332-b837-256792817dde" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Common Logarithms of Fractions and Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "224d1381-d686-5630-b698-51e4184ce621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520040} {:answer/id #uuid "5fe9c910-5c4a-5b61-b6ca-b8292de50985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520140} {:answer/id #uuid "8126d526-06d8-51a6-b4ed-2154d37274ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520178} {:answer/id #uuid "b2a9d371-3a76-5637-9906-45dd3663f5fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520240} {:answer/id #uuid "c4100065-f970-51df-abe3-2d4743cff339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2a9d371-3a76-5637-9906-45dd3663f5fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520240} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca4d7a52-ef14-5dda-b65b-bcf28ca1ff04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d37627d8-2221-5b06-8378-80d838ec2dc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-108088" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[5]{10})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $\\sqrt[5]{10}$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[5]{10}={10}^{1/5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[5]{10})=\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/5})\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=\\frac{1}{5}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/5})=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083173 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afb7f5bb-1a71-5bf5-a4a0-1354256be22b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Common Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2878795d-549b-59c9-ab12-604845f198fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520048} {:answer/id #uuid "4f125697-4b57-5a03-b10b-7c12d3222c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520112} {:answer/id #uuid "94caaf5e-9961-580b-a4ff-185ea4d14ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520203} {:answer/id #uuid "ac82dbfa-1a2b-5f4d-84b4-dbc88643360a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520228} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5b568b-c49c-5a58-bd84-6e27e1eaa6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2878795d-549b-59c9-ab12-604845f198fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520048} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cf199aa-796e-5079-8b74-0ffa7fc0270f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dbc275e8-af27-549a-94fa-e61e97b3469b" :question/math-academy-id "q-24882" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t)$ at $t=10.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we substitute $t=10$ into the function. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡(10\\cdot 10) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=2.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})=2+2=4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81e85da-c4ce-5353-9a7b-d18daa4caf7d" :knowledge-point/title "Converting Between Exponential and Logarithmic Form With Common Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96bd64a4-a693-5801-a289-d7188f556814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520204} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3500ce-45b9-5f87-93da-ff417d20739d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{log}⁡(-2)=\\frac{1}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520232} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ac4ee7-f1da-55c7-b937-45bb16de187b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{1}{100})=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520251} {:answer/id #uuid "d197b142-08f6-5694-bdaa-5a735426ca9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{log}⁡100=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520284} {:answer/id #uuid "f635d2ff-c815-5271-95f7-80002177a122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{1}{100})=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f635d2ff-c815-5271-95f7-80002177a122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{1}{100})=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520351} :answer-field/id #uuid "04a0273e-3e34-5845-8894-910743f99cff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f9714aa-ab20-5f59-96d2-702c693f996b" :question/math-academy-id "q-66543" :question/problem "${10}^{-2}=\\frac{1}{100}$ can be expressed as" :question/worked-solution "The common logarithm of $a$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={10}^{x}$ is equivalent to $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${10}^{-2}=\\frac{1}{100}$ with ${10}^{x}=a,$ we get that $a=\\frac{1}{100}$ and $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as $\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{1}{100})=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a81e85da-c4ce-5353-9a7b-d18daa4caf7d" :knowledge-point/title "Converting Between Exponential and Logarithmic Form With Common Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "734a3505-488f-5ba5-9239-344967b390c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{a}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520158} {:answer/id #uuid "a0bd1aec-dd21-5a4f-ba66-229fde497e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}^{a}=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520212} {:answer/id #uuid "afd98edf-6e85-5875-8c8f-2d9f37432080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}=a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520233} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ac3a1f-e268-5637-8d9a-06f8157181fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}^{-2}=a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520241} {:answer/id #uuid "c5edad54-fc0c-5d59-bcb3-b5d7fa508eeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}^{2}=a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afd98edf-6e85-5875-8c8f-2d9f37432080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}=a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520233} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8203a0f-9d9b-5f31-8cf8-b99f535581ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f7974a75-c042-5467-9fad-57099eb48349" :question/math-academy-id "q-66546" :question/problem "What exponential equation is equivalent to the logarithmic equation $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=\\frac{1}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The common logarithm of $a$ is defined as follows:\n\n$\\operatorname{log}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={10}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=\\frac{1}{2}$ with $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=x,$ we get that $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as ${10}^{1/2}=a.$\n\nFinally, since ${10}^{1/2}=\\sqrt{10},$ the equation $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=\\frac{1}{2}$ is equivalent to $\\sqrt{10}=a.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67d294d0-542a-5332-b837-256792817dde" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Common Logarithms of Fractions and Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ce058e3-52b3-583b-a851-b6062cd9d3ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520006} {:answer/id #uuid "1680aa84-06ac-5c02-87f2-0d18f50b616a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520022} {:answer/id #uuid "5480002b-e285-507d-90f5-deb11809b3ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520119} {:answer/id #uuid "b2acd289-dcc6-5cec-9811-76edd35a02ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520242} {:answer/id #uuid "d1db9dba-08d0-5e9e-9cb3-d347e5a711e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1680aa84-06ac-5c02-87f2-0d18f50b616a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520022} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb5c14ac-5329-5c13-b0e7-0bc5f4c03d4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f698077a-723c-5eb7-8769-9b9cd991b10a" :question/math-academy-id "q-66628" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.01)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $0.01$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n0.01={10}^{-2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(0.01)=\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{-2})\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=-2.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{-2})=-2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67d294d0-542a-5332-b837-256792817dde" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Common Logarithms of Fractions and Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c2ab34-4138-5855-8a4e-101598dd9193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520004} {:answer/id #uuid "17d4deb3-c101-560d-a0fe-7c458fa8e2a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520026} {:answer/id #uuid "550a6942-17ea-5385-abae-07d76741ee8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520121} {:answer/id #uuid "757aaed2-a281-5680-b380-6d10e926d7f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520160} {:answer/id #uuid "b1191e60-4b41-53b9-9363-a5083c3b9e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "757aaed2-a281-5680-b380-6d10e926d7f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520160} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3c10359-a725-56d7-95af-b4b16edd4bab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "091b6406-ea9f-5edd-85ff-748cd7849985" :question/math-academy-id "q-66630" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{10})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite $\\sqrt[{}^{3}]{10}$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{10}={10}^{1/3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{10})=\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/3})\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/3})=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60270e0c-a60c-5a5f-8993-3d8362081c8f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions Containing Common Logarithms Using a Calculator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "555bf3e6-16d1-5155-b677-d1d614176b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.004" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520122} {:answer/id #uuid "56228795-7d2f-53bb-bf44-1e1c61aeaaa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.014" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520127} {:answer/id #uuid "85e682e6-14f1-5c54-90be-cb8eb7b16c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.401" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520186} {:answer/id #uuid "d4481b14-72e5-5219-9cd6-a49808fa8636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520290} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f3f233-eea1-5a76-9baf-466f825d91e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.018" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3f3f233-eea1-5a76-9baf-466f825d91e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.018" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520322} :answer-field/id #uuid "08659010-ed5d-5324-bfa0-6bd93f1094a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0714c123-409e-586b-bfd3-01ab5d4541d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-78745" :question/problem "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, find the value of $f(x)=3\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)$ at $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we replace $x=3$ and get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(2\\cdot 3)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe compute the required value to $3$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate steps to $6$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(15) \\\\  & ≈3(0.778\\,151)-2(1.176\\,091) \\\\  & =2.334\\,453-2.352\\,182 \\\\  & =-0.017\\,729 \\\\  & ≈-0.018\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60270e0c-a60c-5a5f-8993-3d8362081c8f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions Containing Common Logarithms Using a Calculator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06947b56-6c63-577a-9939-3751fd944d34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.308" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520002} {:answer/id #uuid "adebb719-c4b1-5c7f-93ff-0753b8468307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.289" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520231} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ef1288-9185-54f8-a494-ce9ff1450ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.211" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520273} {:answer/id #uuid "dfd49abf-6780-5dcd-92e9-42ff9d78d77d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.296" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520315} {:answer/id #uuid "e491dfee-0a87-5bf1-b4bd-3a44c6127c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.223" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adebb719-c4b1-5c7f-93ff-0753b8468307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.289" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520231} :answer-field/id #uuid "d53df081-5098-54e4-9ae1-62c7e1d21714" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a64a8e4-76a1-5b39-9c41-0b568b095115" :question/math-academy-id "q-99890" :question/problem "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, $\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(8)}{3\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the required expression to $3$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate steps to $6$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(8)}{3\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)} & ≈\\frac{0.903\\,090}{3(1.041\\,393)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.903\\,090}{3.124\\,179} \\\\  & ≈0.289\\,065 \\\\  & ≈0.289\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
